+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start`. The port defaults to 11222 and can be
+overridden with `PORT`.
+
+The server sends a `Permissions-Policy` header allowing this site's origin to
+request resources on the user's local network and loopback interface. It includes
+the legacy `local-network-access` directive for older browsers.
+
+Local network access still requires the user's browser permission. Serve the app
+over HTTPS in production (localhost is suitable for local development). Local
+services must allow the app's origin through CORS when JavaScript needs to read
+their responses. If the app is embedded across origins, its parent must also
+delegate these permissions through its policy and iframe `allow` attribute.
+
+When deploying through a different static host, configure it to send the same
+HTTP header; this policy cannot be configured with an HTML meta tag:
+
+```http
+Permissions-Policy: local-network=(self), loopback-network=(self), local-network-access=(self)
+```
+
+See the [Local Network Access specification](https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/#permissions).
